# Operational Framework for a Machine Learning Engineer (MLE) Role

## 1. Operational Artifacts an MLE Uses Daily

Based on internal documentation and established MLOps practices at Atlassian and industry-wide, the following artifacts form the MLE's daily operational toolkit:

### Model Cards & Documentation
- **Model Cards**: Structured documents capturing model metadata — purpose, intended use, training data, performance metrics, known limitations, fairness assessments, and ownership. At Atlassian, model metadata is tracked in **ML Registry (Tarot v3)** and the **Model Serving Platform (MSP)**, which serves as the system of record for model versions, deployment configs, and lineage. [End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202046686c7c93274f379403a2283d58293f/pages/6708596091/End-to-End+ML+Framework+Atlassian)
- **Model Owner Guides**: Deployment checklists that include compliance verification (model shows as compliant), config.pbtxt validation, unit tests, legal/privacy sign-off, and ML Registry component/version references. [Model Owner Guides](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~712020a570c71e24c846068af97060212d4544/pages/6894978116/Model+Owner+Guides)

### Experiment Tracking Logs
- **MLflow Experiments**: Centralized tracking of training runs in Databricks, logging hyperparameters, metrics, model artifacts, git metadata (commit hash, branch), run parameters, and version labels. MLflow serves as the primary experiment tracking and model packaging tool. [End-to-End ML Framework @ Atlassian](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202046686c7c93274f379403a2283d58293f/pages/6708596091/End-to-End+ML+Framework+Atlassian)
- **Evaluation Reports**: Generated from frameworks like Rovo-eval, AIX-eval, or the Local Evaluations Framework for Stratus. These log per-step metrics (status, latency), aggregated metrics (accuracy, latency percentiles p50/p90/p95/p99), token usage, and tool invocation precision/recall. [Design Doc: Local Evaluations Framework for Stratus](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/gai/pages/6371325263/Design+Doc+Local+Evaluations+Framework+for+Stratus)

### Training Run Manifests
- **Workflow descriptors**: ML Studio workflows define the complete training configuration — modules, datasets, compute targets, parameters, and environment. A training run produces logged model artifacts, validation metrics, and model versions registered in MLflow. [ML Studio: ML Workflow](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/4214128835/ML+Studio+ML+Workflow)
- **Service Descriptors** (`.sd.yml`): Configuration files that define model deployment including version tags per environment (ddev, staging, prod), endpoint mappings, and compute infrastructure. [Abacus Operations Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/teamce24763940c645e2880667b0495ad8e2/pages/6759747113/Abacus+Operations+Runbook)

### A/B Test Design Documents
- **Experiment design docs**: Define hypothesis, control/variant groups, sample size, duration, key metrics, and statistical significance thresholds. [A/B Experiment Analysis](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~511612102/pages/5634459203/A+B+Experiment+Analysis)
- **Interleaving flights**: An alternative to A/B testing for search ranking experiments using CLIP metrics for faster, side-by-side comparison with minimal user impact. [Interleaving Flights](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/CAIMT/blog/2025/10/22/5983656325/Interleaving+Flights+A+Faster+Alternative+to+A+B+and+Shadow+Testing+for+Relevance+Experiments)

### Data Quality Dashboards & Feature Importance
- **Feature store monitoring**: Tecton (being deprecated) and MLFS provide dashboards for feature freshness, data drift, and serving latency. [MLFS & Tecton](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TCH1/pages/5576660473/MLFS+Tecton)
- **Operational dashboards**: Unified dashboards combining operational + ML metrics and cost (within Databricks or web apps), prediction distributions, feature distributions, and data quality checks. [MLOPs@CoreML Long Term Plan](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202089f42605e1d342df8e8011fe153d216f/pages/5783505356/MLOPs+CoreML+Long+Term+Plan)

### Deployment Runbooks
- **Operations runbooks**: Complete guides for model deployment (ONNX export → MLflow register → transition to prod → SageMaker pipeline → SD config update → test each env), monitoring, troubleshooting, cache sync, and capacity planning. [Abacus Operations Runbook](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/teamce24763940c645e2880667b0495ad8e2/pages/6759747113/Abacus+Operations+Runbook)

