## 3. Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) and Guardrails

### Model Validation Gates Before Deployment

The Atlassian ML ecosystem enforces a multi-gate validation process:

1. **Pre-deployment checks** (Stage 1 – Build & Validate):
   - Model registered in ML Registry and shows as compliant
   - Config.pbtxt validated locally in Launchpad
   - Unit tests passed with proof-of-notebook (basic inference, empty optional fields, edge case tests)
   - Legal/Privacy sign-off obtained
   - Unique subfolder naming verified
   - Model packaged as Triton module in ML Studio

2. **Quality gates** (CI/CD):
   - Lint & type check (ruff, mypy)
   - Unit tests (pytest)
   - Vulnerability scan (pip-audit, Snyk)
   - Data schema validation (Great Expectations, pandera)
   - Evaluate model metrics against thresholds and previous production model
   - Block promotion if accuracy/F1 below threshold

3. **Post-deployment validation**:
   - Run on subset of customer traffic or in shadow mode
   - Integration tests against deployed endpoint
   - Load testing (k6 or locust): ramp 10→40→80req/sec, watch latency/error rate/CPU/host count
   - Verify autoscaling within 5min of sustained load

[CI/CD for MLOps](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/~6359788e1cc605b1fd1664ec/pages/6726837663/CI+CD+for+MLOps)
[MSP Validation Workflow](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/3372518966/MSP+Validation+Workflow+Initial+Thoughts)

### Format Safety Guardrails
- **Blocked formats**: Pickle (.pkl), PyTorch (.pt), Keras (.h5) are blocked from production deployment via format validation gates in Tarot Platform, Tarot SDK, and Teamserve. [COMMIT-27251](https://hello.jira.atlassian.cloud/browse/COMMIT-27251)
- **Safe formats**: ONNX is the preferred model format for deployment (splitting >400MB models into structure + weights files)

### Canary / Shadow Deployment Procedures
- **Progressive environment rollout**: ddev → staging → prod (managed by Spinnaker)
- **Shadow mode**: Models make predictions in parallel to champion model without serving to users
- **Canary rollout**: Deploy to subset of traffic, monitor for P95 latency increase >10% or error rate >0.5%
- **Automated rollback**: Roll back if canary metrics breach thresholds
- **AZ rotation audit**: Canary AZ rotation order must be audited and spread (per Tony's own recent work: OPP-202605-09)

### Data Quality Checks
- Feature distribution monitoring for skew/drift vs. training data
- Feature freshness checks (streaming features stale detection)
- Data schema validation at pipeline ingestion
- Automated retraining triggers when drift thresholds are breached

### Bias/Fairness Audits
- AI/ML Enablement team works with model owners to "remove model bias and address ethics and algorithm fairness challenges"
- Legal and Privacy sign-off required before deployment (contact: Privacy → Julia Shu; Legal → Samson Chen)

### On-Call Responsibilities for Model Incidents
- **On-call DE model**: Close Opsgenie alerts, resolve failures in jobs/services, monitor disturbed channels, communicate to impacted users, create HOT incidents if needed, escalate to SME orEM, conduct weekly post-on-call retros. [AI DE Oncall Support Model](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/APD2/pages/6330236128/AI+DE+Oncall+Support+Model)
- **Escalation path**: Primary on-call → SME escalation → Engineering Manager → Incident (Sev3) at72 hours
- **Rollback SOP**: Safe-rollback wrapper script that preserves ASG floor (per Tony's OPP-202605-11)

