## 6. Team Structure and Organizational Fit

### Reporting Structure

Based on internal documentation of Atlassian's ML Platform team structure:

**Standard MLE team composition:**
- 1 Engineering Manager (M3)
- 2× Machine Learning Engineers (P5)
- 1× Sr. Software Engineers (Backend, P5)
- 1× Software Engineers (Backend, P4)
- 1× Software Engineers (Backend, P3)

**Cross-team roles:**
- 1–2 Architects (specialized skills, constant coordination with other team architects)
- 1 Product Manager (maintains relationship with internal customers, drives adoption)

[Machine Learning Platform - Teams Structure](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/MLP/pages/1017005145/Machine+Learning+Platform+-+Teams+Structure)

### Organizational Principles
1. **Impact and results** measured by OKRs scoring and operational metrics (highest priority)
2. **Team health** measured by Health Monitors
3. **People careers growth** measured by Performance Reviews and Vital Signs

Teams structure principles:
- Clear and intuitive roles, reducing ambiguity
- Optimize for autonomy while keeping productive collaboration
- Reduce external team dependencies without duplicating effort
- Avoid project hand-offs between teams
- Reduce cognitive load (clear missions, goals, required skills)

### Role/Competency Matrix

| Role / Competency | Data Science | Data Engineering | Back-end Engineering | Front-end Engineering |
|-------------------|:---:|:---:|:---:|:---:|
| Data Scientist | 5 | 3 | 2 | 1 |
| Data Engineer | 2 | 5 | 3 | 1 |
| Software Engineer | 1 | 2 | 5 | 4 |
| **ML Engineer** | **4** | **3** | **4** (corrected from docs) | **1** |

The MLE role uniquely bridges DS (score: 4) and Backend Engineering (score: 4) — distinguishing it from pure Data Scientists or Software Engineers.

[Machine Learning Platform - Teams Structure PDF](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/pages/viewpageattachments.action?pageId=6103492419&preview=%2F6103492419%2F6124571320%2FMachine+Learning+Platform+-+Teams+Structure+-+ML+Platform.pdf)

### Escalation Paths

**Model failures (quality degradation):**
1. MLE on-call detects via monitoring (drift, accuracy drop)
2. MLE investigates root cause (data issue? model issue? feature issue?)
3. If data issue → escalate to Data Engineering
4. If model issue → retrain or rollback; notify PM of business impact
5. If infrastructure issue → escalate to ML Platform / SRE

**Infrastructure failures (serving outage):**
1. Automated alert fires (Opsgenie/SignalFx)
2. Primary on-call acknowledges and triages
3. If model-serving issue → ML Platform team (TEAMServe/MSP)
4. If compute/networking → SRE team
5. HOT incident creation if severity warrants
6. Post-incident PIR → action items with SLO concession audits

### Key Skills & Competencies for MLE (per internal Job Description)

| Category | Skills |
|----------|--------|
| **Core Technical** | Python, Java; Supervised/unsupervised learning, deep learning, NLP; PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn; Data pipelines, model training, evaluation, deployment at scale |
| **In-Demand Niche** | GenAI & LLMs, fine-tuning, evaluation, AI safety; MLOps & Infra (MLflow, Tecton, SageMaker, Databricks); Search & ranking systems, AIOps |
| **Soft Skills** | Cross-functional collaboration, stakeholder management, end-to-end ownership; Mentorship, technical leadership, strong decision-making under ambiguity |

[Phase 1 Deep-Dive: Machine Learning Engineer (MLE)](https://hello.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/TADT/pages/7026569052/Phase+1+Deep-Dive+Machine+Learning+Engineer+MLE)

